    "narrative": "The analytical model identifies **Mickey Moniak** (75.18) and **James Wood** (75.13) as our premier starts for today\u2019s slate. **Mickey Moniak** is in a prime position to capitalize on a +14% park factor and a significant platoon edge against Peralta, while the generous 92% SB-conversion probability against a slow-delivery pitcher makes him a high-leverage target for our primary scarcity category. Similarly, **James Wood** benefits from a high-efficiency leadoff spot and a favorable matchup against Ober, where his xwOBA of .377 suggests he is poised to outperform the raw projection. We are also leaning heavily into **Brice Turang** (66.93) and **Trevor Story** (63.18); **Brice Turang** remains a must-start due to the synergy between his 85% SB-conversion rate and the current pitching matchup, while **Trevor Story** provides surprising stability in the four-hole against Flaherty.\n\nNavigating the bottom of the order and bench decisions proved difficult today, particularly with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (48.20) serving as our most notable bench omission. **Vinnie Pasquantino** sat just outside the active threshold primarily due to a -15% dynamic platoon penalty against the southpaw Cantillo, pushing his efficiency score below that of **Austin Riley** (48.84), who clings to a spot despite a tougher matchup against Woo. We are keeping a close watch on the **Jose Caballero** situation; he was firmly excluded due to a combination of an inefficient bottom-of-the-order slot and a 45% rain risk, which carries too much volatility for our current roster construction. While **Gabriel Moreno** (42.12) is officially starting, his proximity to the floor is concerning given Skenes\u2019s elite 3.04 xERA, and we will monitor the situation closely to ensure we do not burn unnecessary game caps if the game flow turns sour early.",
